{
  "about": "Cross-port fixture set for the endpoint PEP decision (stellar-core-go/policy). Inputs -> expected decision. Hand-authored from the Python spec stellar_core/policy.py plus the 2026-10-03 plan amendment (the gateway _meta principal); NOT a recorded tape, because the Go port deliberately diverges (see divergences). A TypeScript or Rust port replays the same cases. Peers are SPIFFE ids typed by the fleet rule (mtls.PeerFromRequest): star subject is the bare name, session/human subject the full id; empty = no certificate.",
  "sidecars": "testdata/sidecars/<name>.orbit.toml, copied verbatim from foundry-stocks/orbits (frozen, feff611)",
  "divergences": [
    "reason names: no_edge / verb_not_on_edge / unidentified / edge_allows replace Python no_contract / verb_not_in_contract / unidentified_caller / contract_allows; no_acl is new (Python cannot run without an ACL)",
    "the verdict is consult, not deny, for a non-star caller: Python marks pdp_not_consulted as would_deny=True; here the plane was not asked, so the record says what would be asked, not what would be refused",
    "the gateway path is new: a verified hades peer with a hades/principal-type stamp in _meta takes the non-service path with the stamped principal; Python has no gateway rule",
    "a verb is matched exactly as served (bare); a prefixed-form name is a different verb and is not on the edge. Python matches the verb as given too, but a star here no longer knows its gateway prefix",
    "a missing sidecar is a decision (no_acl), not a constructor error, so witness mode boots without one",
    "ACL parse: an absent status is not approved (Python: approved); two blocks for one consumer is an error (Python: last wins); a non-string version is an error (Python ignores version)",
    "the consult is ASKED in witness mode when a PDP is configured (STELLAR_PDP_URL): the plane's answer is recorded as allow{pdp_allows} or deny{pdp_denies} (rendered would_deny), and a plane that did not answer as pdp_error with the client's fault posture as the verdict (fail-open: allow); Python never consults in witness mode. The star asks the endpoint_decision document with its own name and the verb as served; the bundle joins the gateway prefix (prefix_verb, as hades aggregates it) from the roster, and only the action discriminator of the arguments crosses (pdp_cases, action_cases)"
  ],
